  "task_id": "tmm_optimize_a_21_layer_dielectric_bandpass_filter_o_8f8821f612",
  "user_request_original": "Optimize a 21-layer dielectric bandpass filter on CaF2 substrate using Ge (high-index) and ZnS (low-index) materials in a three-cavity Fabry-Perot topology. Initialize cavity layer thicknesses near theoretical half-wave resonance values (λ/2n) at 4.45 μm center wavelength, and mirror section thicknesses near quarter-wave values (λ/4n). Enforce hard thickness bounds of 50-500 nm per layer. Seed 40% of initial population with deterministic λ/4n multiples for mirror sections. Optimize for high transmittance in 4.15-4.35 μm and 4.55-4.75 μm passbands, low transmittance in 3.60-4.00 μm and 4.85-5.20 μm stopbands, at normal incidence in air. Use gradient-based thickness optimizer with resonance-centered initialization. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 3600-4000 nm, 4150-4350 nm, 4550-4750 nm, 4850-5200 nm. soft objectives: high transmittance in 4.15-4.35 um and 4.55-4.75 um bands; low transmittance in 3.60-4.00 um and 4.85-5.20 um bands. behaviors to suppress or avoid: high transmittance in stopbands; high reflectance in passbands. manufacturing constraints: no metal layers; maximum 24 layers; conventional depositable infrared inorganic dielectric materials.",
  "normalized_request_english": "The system shall optimize a 21-layer alternating Ge/ZnS dielectric bandpass filter on CaF2 at normal incidence. Transmittance is maximized in the 4.15-4.35 um and 4.55-4.75 um passbands while being minimized in the 3.60-4.00 um and 4.85-5.20 um stopbands. All 21 finite layer thicknesses are optimized within 50-500 nm bounds using gradient descent, initialized near lambda/4n and lambda/2n values at 4.45 um.",
